    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Clinical features, morphology, immunohistochemistry, and genetics of tumours with a follicular growth pattern arising in the head and neck region</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "German Ott",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;<strong>Characteristic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.05pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Classic&nbsp;follicular lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Paediatric-type follicular lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>IRF4</em>-rearranged large B-cell lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often systemic nodal disease</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Middle-aged and elderly patients</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Localized nodal disease (stage&nbsp;I/II)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Children and young adults, rare in elderly</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Localized extranodal (tonsillar) or nodal disease (stage&nbsp;I/II)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Children and young adults, rare in elderly</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Morphology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Atypical monotonous follicular structures</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mainly centrocytes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Purely follicular proliferation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large expansile follicles</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often intermediate-sized cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Follicular, follicular and diffuse, or purely diffuse</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large expansile follicles</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Medium-sized to large tumour cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunohistochemistry</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD10+, BCL2+</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Low Ki-67 index</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD10+, BCL2&minus;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High Ki-67 index</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD10+/&minus;, BCL2+/&minus;, IRF4&nbsp;(MUM1) strongly positive</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High Ki-67 index</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Genetics</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.05pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">t(14;18)-positive<em> KMT2D</em>, <em>TNFRSF14</em>, <em>CREBBP</em>, and <em>EZH2</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Clonal B-cell proliferation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No <em>BCL2, BCL6</em>, <em>IRF4</em>, or IGH rearrangements</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>IRF8</em>, <em>TNFRSF14</em>, and <em>MAP2K1</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cryptic <em>IRF4</em>/IGH (rare IGL) rearrangement in 70%</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>CARD11</em>, <em>CD79B</em>, and <em>MYD88 </em>mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 58441,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 241,
    "fileId": 27203,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Salivary gland follicular lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The parotid salivary gland has been overrun by a malignant proliferation of atypical lymphoid cells, expanding into the adjacent parenchyma and soft tissue. There are numerous expanded follicles, showing enlarged cells with increased N:C&nbsp;ratio. The chromatin is coarse, with small nucleoli noted. Tingible-body macrophages are absent.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/27203.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
